{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789496196,"nonce":"X5ybrOmgx/QkFN4bLRSEoqcOQTA=","title":"Class body statements other than methods","message":"deltablue and hexiom2 declare attributes in the class body (`class Strength: REQUIRED = 0`, tables of constants, class-level lists) and read them as `Class.NAME` and `self.NAME`. The frontend refuses any class body statement that is not a method. A class attribute assigned once from a literal is a module-level constant under the class's name; one that is reassigned, or read through `self` and shadowed by an instance attribute, needs the class to carry it as a field with the default. Gap list 89aaf85.","files":null}]}